  <prompt>
    Author the **integration-heavy vertical-slice seam tests** for the messaging channel per ADR-038, and PRESERVE the existing email-inbound matching behavior under characterization tests. Per NFR-08 the pyramid is integration-heavy; per ADR-038 the seam-level end-to-end tests live under `tests/integration/seam/**` (the vertical-slice-seam category is the DoD for dispatch-spine changes).

    Cover these vertical slices (each a real end-to-end path through the shipped code, boundary-mocked only at true external edges per ADR-038):

    1. **Messaging send/archive slice** (FR-01/FR-04/051) — outbound send dispatches through the channel dispatcher by `CommunicationType.Message`, persists exactly one `sprk_communication` (thread set), and the archiver writes a transcript artifact to SPE. Assert echo-dedup: the Event Grid echo of our own message is a no-op (idempotent on ACS message id) — sending once yields exactly one persisted record.
    2. **Inbound ingest slice** (FR-02/031/NFR-03) — an inbound ACS `ChatMessageReceivedInThread` event flows webhook → Service Bus job → normalizer → `MessagingIngestor` persist → enrichment, producing exactly one persisted `sprk_communication`; **duplicate delivery yields one record** (idempotent on ACS message id); repeated failure dead-letters.
    3. **`IThreadResolver` slice** (FR-06/040) — the direction-symmetric resolver: an email reply joins its parent's thread; a chat message joins its ACS thread; a fresh outbound message/email creates a thread.
    4. **Privacy enforcement slice** (FR-08/042/NFR-06) — a private thread's messages are invisible to a user without a grant; an internal-only message is invisible to non-internal users; flipping a thread to open exposes only messages from that point forward (point-forward).

    **Characterization guard (mandatory, NFR-08):** BEFORE the `IThreadResolver` extension is exercised, capture the EXISTING email inbound matching behavior as characterization tests and assert it stays green after (Success Criterion 4). If the email-r4 suite already covers this, extend/reference it (do NOT clone per ADR-038); if a gap exists, add the characterization test.

    Follow ADR-038 strictly: NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, NO DI-registration tests, NO ctor null-check tests; boundary mocks only; `TimeProvider` over `Stopwatch`. Tests are the deliverable — no product code change.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke test engineer authoritative on ADR-038 (integration-heavy pyramid, 7 KEEP-path categories, `tests/integration/seam/**` vertical-slice-seam DoD, banned mock patterns) and the shipped Communication spine (channel dispatcher, ingestor, thread resolver, privacy filter). Writes vertical-slice seam tests + characterization guards; does not modify product code.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Vertical-slice seam tests exist (under `tests/integration/seam/**` where end-to-end, `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` where unit-appropriate) covering messaging send/archive (echo-dedup), inbound ingest (idempotency + DLQ), `IThreadResolver` (both directions + fresh-thread), and privacy enforcement (private/internal-only/point-forward). Existing email inbound matching is captured/referenced as characterization tests and stays green. All tests follow ADR-038 (no banned mock patterns; boundary mocks only). `dotnet test` green; no product code changed.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      NFR-08 makes the test pyramid integration-heavy and specifically calls for vertical-slice seam tests for the new channel (send/archive/ingest), the `IThreadResolver`, and privacy enforcement, while preserving existing email inbound matching under characterization tests before extending. email-r4 established the pattern: task 017 added spine seam tests under `tests/integration/seam/Communication/` and per-rung tests by reference (no clone). Mirror that — this task adds the SECOND channel's seam coverage + the resolver + privacy slices.

      §11 (test surface): reuse the email-r4 seam-test fixtures/harness under `tests/integration/seam/Communication/` rather than standing up a parallel harness; add messaging cases to it. The characterization guard is the load-bearing NFR-08 obligation — the shared `Services/Communication/` edit (040) is the project's highest-risk shared-path change, so the existing email behavior MUST be pinned green before/after.

      ADR-038 bans (enforced by code-review at Step 9.5): no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration-only tests, no ctor null-check tests; use `TimeProvider` not `Stopwatch`; boundary mocks only (ACS SDK client, Service Bus, SPE store, Dataverse client at their true seams).
    </background>
