  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read ADR-038 (KEEP-path categories, `tests/integration/seam/**`, banned patterns), `TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md`, `tests/CLAUDE.md`, and the existing `tests/integration/seam/Communication/` harness (from email-r4 task 017). Read the shipped surfaces under test (031 ingestor/normalizer/job, 040 resolver, 042 privacy filter, 020/051 send/archive dispatch).</step>
    <step order="2">Characterization guard FIRST: locate the existing email inbound matching tests. If they pin the behavior the 040 resolver extension touches, reference/extend them; if a gap exists, add characterization tests capturing current email inbound matching. Run them green as the baseline (NFR-08 / Success Criterion 4).</step>
    <step order="3">Author the messaging send/archive slice (FR-01/04): send dispatches by `CommunicationType.Message`; exactly one persisted record; archiver writes the transcript to SPE (boundary-mock SPE); echo-dedup no-op (idempotent on ACS message id).</step>
    <step order="4">Author the inbound ingest slice (FR-02/031/NFR-03): webhook → job → normalizer → `MessagingIngestor` persist → enrichment; exactly one record; duplicate delivery → one record; repeated failure → DLQ. Boundary-mock Service Bus + ACS client; `TimeProvider` for any timing.</step>
    <step order="5">Author the `IThreadResolver` slice (FR-06/040): email reply joins parent's thread; chat message joins ACS thread; fresh outbound message/email creates a thread; direction-symmetric.</step>
    <step order="6">Author the privacy enforcement slice (FR-08/042/NFR-06): private-thread invisibility without a grant; internal-only invisibility to non-internal users; point-forward open exposes only post-switch messages; ACS membership never exceeds Dataverse-derived access.</step>
    <step order="7">Verify NO banned patterns (grep for `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration-only tests, ctor null-check tests); place seam end-to-end tests under `tests/integration/seam/**`, unit-appropriate cases under `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test` (targeted: Communication + seam filters, then the broad Communication suite) — all green, including the characterization baseline before + after.</step>
    <step order="9.5">Step 9.5 (UNCONDITIONAL per TEST-MODIFYING): `code-review` on the new tests (focus: ADR-038 compliance, no banned mocks, boundary-only, characterization guard present); `adr-check` against ADR-038 + `spec.md` (NFR-08, NFR-03, NFR-06). Address Critical findings.</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (080 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (which slices are seam vs unit, characterization approach [extend vs new], boundary mocks used, test count).</step>
  </steps>

